    "field": "Numerical weather prediction",
    "problem": "The high computational cost of promising new-generation global models has limited their application to a few case studies, preventing a proper statistical evaluation of their skill in predicting the Madden-Julian Oscillation (MJO) compared to operational forecast models.",
    "method": "A series of simulations are conducted using a supercomputer-powered, new-generation global model (NICAM) that explicitly resolves cloud systems to statistically evaluate its prediction skill for the Madden-Julian Oscillation and demonstrate its effectiveness for month-long tropical forecasts.",
    "task": "The task is to statistically evaluate the Madden-Julian Oscillation (MJO) prediction skill of a new-generation, computationally expensive global cloud-resolving model by conducting a large series of simulations on a supercomputer.",
